  "caption": "Quinn read that you must sit up straight or else, so Quinn sat like a statue for four hours — and ended up with a back like cardboard. Next stop: a pricey posture gadget.\n\nResearch suggests there's no single perfect posture, and posture alone is a poor predictor of pain. Your spine is strong and built to move.\n\nWhat can help: change positions often, get up every 30–45 minutes, build strength and capacity, and during a flare simply use whatever positions feel comfy. Posture correctors often aren't needed.\n\nGet it checked if pain keeps hanging around, you have a diagnosed spinal condition, or symptoms get worse despite changes.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
